WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.516
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Question 1

00:00:03.063 --> 00:00:07.528
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> OK, so you need to calculate two thirds of 18%.

00:00:07.782 --> 00:00:14.579
First, you need to find one third – so, divide 18 by 3, which equals 6, and then,

00:00:14.579 --> 00:00:19.690
to find two thirds, you multiply 6 by 2, which equals 12.

00:00:19.722 --> 00:00:21.984
So, the answer is 12%.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.229
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Question 2

00:00:26.166 --> 00:00:27.526
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> To answer this question,

00:00:27.811 --> 00:00:31.657
you need to know the formula for calculating the area of a circle,

00:00:31.657 --> 00:00:35.379
which is ‘pi multiplied by r squared’.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:44.819
The value of pi is 3.14 ‘r’ equals the radius of a circle and you can find the radius easily

00:00:44.819 --> 00:00:50.164
because it’s half the diameter of the flowerbed, which is 3.9 metres.

00:00:50.616 --> 00:00:57.555
So, the radius is 1.95. Squared means multiplied by itself.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:05.921
So – you may need a calculator for this – 1.95 squared is 3.8, to the nearest decimal point.

00:01:06.096 --> 00:01:13.701
Multiply this by pi – 3.14 – and you get 11.9 to the nearest decimal point.

00:01:13.867 --> 00:01:17.838
So, the answer is 11.9 square metres.

00:01:19.752 --> 00:01:21.047
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Question 3

00:01:22.065 --> 00:01:25.721
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Most countries use metric measurements, for example,

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.165
metres, centimetres, grams, kilos, etc.

00:01:29.602 --> 00:01:36.562
Apart from the UK, only the USA, Liberia, and Myanmar use imperial measurements.

00:01:37.125 --> 00:01:42.871
In the UK, both are used, but imperial measurements are often preferred,

00:01:42.896 --> 00:01:48.823
for example, distances are given in miles, beer is sold in pints or half pints,

00:01:48.822 --> 00:01:52.374
and petrol is sold in both litres and gallons.

00:01:52.374 --> 00:01:56.291
So, the answer here is 3.5 inches.

00:01:56.759 --> 00:02:02.558
An inch is an imperial unit of length and is roughly equivalent to two and a half centimetres.

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:05.615
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Question 4

00:02:06.473 --> 00:02:08.909
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> To calculate the volume of a box,

00:02:08.909 --> 00:02:16.536
you simply multiply the width by the height by the length, so 3 multiplied by 5,

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:21.810
which equals 15, multiplied by 8 which equals 120.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.710
So, the answer is 120 cubic centimetres.

00:02:27.742 --> 00:02:29.001
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Question 5

00:02:30.056 --> 00:02:35.839
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Here we know, by adding 2, that April 16th is a Thursday.

00:02:36.244 --> 00:02:44.454
By adding 7 each time, we can see that April 23rd and April 30th are also Thursdays,

00:02:44.556 --> 00:02:50.101
so the last Thursday is April 30th, also the last day of the month.

00:02:50.562 --> 00:02:54.631
This means that none of the options given for the answers is right.

00:02:56.551 --> 00:02:57.855
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Question 6

00:02:58.808 --> 00:03:05.444
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> So, according to the question, for every 5 parts of flour we need 2 parts of sugar.

00:03:05.738 --> 00:03:09.705
So, first we need to calculate how much 1 part is.

00:03:10.098 --> 00:03:19.782
If 5 parts equals a total of 200 grams, then 1 part equals 200 divided by 5, which makes 40.

00:03:19.992 --> 00:03:26.967
Then, to calculate 2 parts, we just multiply 40 by 2, so the answer is 80 grams.

00:03:28.808 --> 00:03:30.184
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Question 7

00:03:31.215 --> 00:03:35.169
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> Each pie chart shows the sales at one of the cinemas.

00:03:35.408 --> 00:03:41.533
If we look at the sections of the pie chart showing Child tickets, that is, the green sections,

00:03:41.667 --> 00:03:47.633
we can see that for the Galaxy Cinema, the green section is larger than for the Palace Cinema.

00:03:47.745 --> 00:03:51.102
So, the manager’s claim is ‘definitely true’.

00:03:53.087 --> 00:03:54.315
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> Question 8

00:03:55.339 --> 00:04:00.012
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> First, we need to calculate the total number of accidents in the week,

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:06.073
which is 5 on Monday, 15 on Tuesday, 19 on Wednesday,

00:04:06.121 --> 00:04:12.930
5 on Thursday, 16 on Friday, 3 on Saturday, and 7 on Sunday.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:22.275
Add all of those together – 5 plus 15 is 20, plus 19 makes 39, plus 5 makes 44,

00:04:22.275 --> 00:04:29.868
plus 16 makes 60, plus 3 makes 63, plus 7 equals 70.

00:04:30.074 --> 00:04:33.705
So, the total number of accidents is 70.

00:04:34.142 --> 00:04:38.338
Now we have to calculate the number of serious or major accidents,

00:04:38.394 --> 00:04:41.701
which are shown by the blue sections on the bar chart.

00:04:42.171 --> 00:04:52.677
So, starting from Monday, we have 2, 3, 5, 2, 6, none on Saturday, and finally 3.

00:04:53.209 --> 00:05:02.076
If we add those together, we get 21. So, we need to know what 21 is as a percentage of 70.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:10.881
The easiest way to do that is to divide 21 by 70, which is 0.3, and then multiply by 100,

00:05:10.882 --> 00:05:12.788
which makes 30%.

00:05:12.851 --> 00:05:15.150
Or, if you’re using a calculator,

00:05:15.222 --> 00:05:20.844
21 divided by 70 and press the percentage button, and the answer is 30%.